[HOLE 2] D2D RX deskew FIFO — the narrow exception constraints.sdc:358 asks for

WHAT THIS DOES
    Appends one block to tidelink_constraints.sdc. No existing line is changed.

    set_false_path  +5   (all -to NAMED PINS: 4 demet groups crossing INTO
                          out_clk + 1 crossing back out; 152 pins in the
                          shipping build)
    set_max_delay   +1   (payload: 4096 mem_l cells, 10.0 ns)
    set_min_delay   +1   (payload: explicit 0 — the half that matters)
    set_clock_groups  0  (UNCHANGED — no clock-to-clock exception is added)

WHY
    constraints.sdc:358-362 leaves this open by name:
      "[OWNER, DO NOT LET THIS SLIDE] ... across u_deskew, which is an async
       FIFO. This one probably DOES want a narrow set_false_path on the FIFO's
       data path only - not a blanket group cut."

    All 16 RX clocks are in ONE async group, and set_clock_groups never cuts
    within a group (constraints.sdc:349-354, deliberate), so the FIFO is timed
    today. Because all eight word clocks are -source TL_CLK_RX -divide_by 16
    they carry IDENTICAL waveforms, so setup gets the full 160 ns and is never
    the issue — but HOLD gets a ZERO-ns budget against whatever lane-to-lane
    skew CTS actually built, and CTS built the lanes very differently:
    reports/cts_clock_trees.rep:185-192, D2D_RX_WORDN_CLK_0 has 501 clock gates
    against 36 for each of lanes 1-7. The hold fixer chases that skew across
    4096 FIFO memory flops and a 32:1 read mux, threading buffers into the
    receive datapath of the one interface with a known marginal-eye failure.

CORRECTION TO THE NOTE THIS CLOSES
    constraints.sdc:359 names the crossing "D2D_RX_CLK_0 -> D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_n".
    That is not the FIFO. WavD2DGpio_v2.v:897-928 wires
    u_deskew.lane_clk = {gpiorx_7..0}_io_link_clk and u_deskew.out_clk =
    gpiorx_0_io_link_clk, so the FIFO crossing is WORD -> WORD:
    D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_n (n=1..7) -> D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_0. Confirmed against the
    shipping build — reports/cts_clock_latency_setup.rep:29-33 names
    `u_deskew_g_lane_write[6].mem_l_reg[26][2]/CP` under `Clock:
    D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_6`. The D2D_RX_CLK_0 -> word paths are real, but they are
    intra-lane inside WavD2DGpioRx and must stay timed. A cut written against
    the clock pair the note names would have missed the FIFO entirely.

THE STRUCTURE, VERIFIED IN THE COMPILED RTL
    tidelink_asic.flist:73 pins tidelink_lane_deskew_v2.sv as the file that
    builds (it declares module tidelink_lane_deskew, :190). That module is the
    textbook pointer-protected async FIFO:
      :529-548  write side, lane_clk[gi]: mem_l[wr_ptr_l] <= lane_data
                                          wr_gray_l <= bin2gray(wr_ptr_l+1)
      :960-972  read side,  out_clk:      wr_gray_sync0 <= wr_gray_flat
                                          wr_gray_sync1 <= wr_gray_sync0
                                          rd_word = mem_l[rd_ptr_l[gi]]
    Its own header (:49) states the intent: "CDC: wr_ptr crosses to out_clk as
    GRAY (RX-audit Finding #2 fix, 2026-06-09)". So: gray-coded pointer +
    two-flop demet, payload unsynchronised. Pointer-protected, confirmed.

    Cut STAGE 0 ONLY. wr_gray_sync1's D is fed by wr_gray_sync0's Q in the same
    domain and IS the metastability settling window — cutting it would destroy
    the protection instead of describing it.

COUNTS, MEASURED IN build/full-20260814/outputs/nanosoc_eth_chiplet_pads_gate.v
    wr_gray_sync0_reg    48   (8 lanes x 6 bits; DEPTH_LOG=5 -> PW=6)  MANDATORY
    sync_idx_sync0_reg   48                                            optional
    sync_seen_sync0_reg   8                                            optional
    sync_dist_sync0_reg  40                                            optional
    clr_meta_l_reg        8   (reverse direction: out_clk -> lane_clk) optional
    mem_l_reg          4096   (8 x 32 entries x 16 bits)               MANDATORY
    The four "optional" groups exist only under SYNC_REANCHOR_EN=1 and are
    generate-pruned otherwise, so absence is a NOTE, not an error. Absence of
    wr_gray_sync0 or mem_l is fatal.

TOOL SUPPORT — VERIFIED, NOT ASSUMED
    set_max_delay -datapath_only DOES NOT EXIST in either tool here, so this
    block does not use it. Genus 21.1 SDC Command Reference lists set_max_delay
    as [-rise] [-fall] [-ignore_clock_latency] [-exception_name] [-comment]
    [-combinational_from_to] [-reset_path]; "datapath_only" appears ZERO times
    in that document. Innovus 21.11 Text Command Reference gives
    `set_max_delay value [-combinational_from_to | -ignore_clock_latency]`.

    Consequence worth recording: the live C2 block at constraints.sdc:568-570
    wraps -datapath_only in `catch`, so in this flow it ALWAYS takes its
    fallback leg and the C2 payload bound is a plain set_max_delay, not the
    datapath-only bound its comment describes. That is SAFE (the fallback is
    stricter) and is deliberately NOT changed by this patch.

    The fc_shell idiom `get_cells -hier -filter {NAME =~ "*a/b*"}` that
    TideLink's block SDC uses is NOT portable here: Genus's -filter `name`
    checks the instance BASE NAME (Genus 21.1 get_cells), so a pattern
    containing `/` returns an empty collection and the constraint silently does
    nothing. This block uses hierarchical-path globs with a candidate ladder
    instead — the form this file has already proven binds (the div_en_r*/Q and
    count_reg[3]/Q anchors, both measured 8/8 at read time).

