READ BEFORE JUDGING THE FIRST RUN
    The block PRINTS what it bound — one `TIDELINK-SDC: deskew ...` line per
    group with a pin/cell count. Read those lines first. They are the difference
    between "the exception landed" and "the exception read as landed".
    Expect: 48 / 48 / 8 / 40 / 8 pins and 4096 cells.

    Baseline to compare hold against: post-route-opt hold WNS -0.001 / TNS
    -0.002 / FEP 7 (reports/hold_05_route_opt.rep). This block should move hold
    endpoints DOWN or leave them flat, and should remove hold buffers from the
    deskew read path. If hold endpoints RISE, the demet cut bound nothing —
    check the printed counts, do not widen the budget.

--- a/ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/tidelink_constraints.sdc
+++ b/ASIC/genus-innovus/inputs/tidelink_constraints.sdc
@@ -715,3 +715,276 @@
 # Drive and load are electrical characterisation; the setup uncertainty needs
 # the far die's source jitter plus package and channel skew, which is a
 # different measurement.
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# [HOLE 2] D2D RX DESKEW FIFO — THE NARROW EXCEPTION
+# ===========================================================================
+# Added 2026-08-18. This is the constraint constraints.sdc:358-362 asks for:
+#
+#   "[OWNER, DO NOT LET THIS SLIDE] ... word<->capture (D2D_RX_CLK_0 ->
+#    D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_n) across u_deskew, which is an async FIFO. This one
+#    probably DOES want a narrow set_false_path on the FIFO's data path only -
+#    not a blanket group cut. Constrain it properly once the first run shows
+#    what it reports."
+#
+# FIRST, CORRECT THE CLOCK PAIR IN THAT NOTE. The deskew FIFO's asynchronous
+# crossing is NOT D2D_RX_CLK_0 -> D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_n. From the port map that is
+# actually compiled (WavD2DGpio_v2.v:897-928, and tidelink_asic.flist:73 pins
+# tidelink_lane_deskew_v2.sv as the module that builds):
+#
+#   u_deskew.lane_clk[7:0] = {gpiorx_7..0}_io_link_clk  = D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_7..0
+#   u_deskew.out_clk       =  gpiorx_0_io_link_clk      = D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_0
+#
+# so the crossing is WORD -> WORD: D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_n (n=1..7) -> _0. Confirmed
+# in the shipping build, not inferred: reports/cts_clock_latency_setup.rep:29-33
+# names `u_deskew_g_lane_write[6].mem_l_reg[26][2]/CP` under `Clock:
+# D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_6`. D2D_RX_CLK_0 -> word paths exist too, but they are inside
+# WavD2DGpioRx (link_data_word -> link_data_reg), NOT across the FIFO, and they
+# are a real synchronous check that must stay timed.
+#
+# WHY IT IS TIMED TODAY. All 16 RX clocks sit in ONE -asynchronous group
+# (constraints.sdc:395, `-group [get_clocks $_rx_grp]`). set_clock_groups cuts
+# BETWEEN groups and never within one, which is the deliberate conservative
+# choice recorded at constraints.sdc:349-354 -- so every path inside the D2D
+# receive domain, this FIFO included, stays timed. Nothing here changes that
+# doctrine: NO clock-to-clock exception is added below. Every exception is
+# -to a NAMED PIN, exactly as the C2 demet block does at constraints.sdc:517-518.
+#
+# THE FIFO IS THE TEXTBOOK POINTER-PROTECTED SHAPE — VERIFIED IN THE RTL:
+#   write side (lane_clk[gi]), tidelink_lane_deskew_v2.sv:529-548
+#     mem_l[wr_ptr_l] <= lane_data[...]      ;# payload, NO synchroniser
+#     wr_gray_l       <= bin2gray(wr_ptr_l+1);# pointer, GRAY (one bit per step)
+#   read side (out_clk), tidelink_lane_deskew_v2.sv:960-972
+#     wr_gray_sync0 <= wr_gray_flat          ;# demet stage 1  <-- ASYNC CAPTURE
+#     wr_gray_sync1 <= wr_gray_sync0         ;# demet stage 2  <-- STAYS TIMED
+#     wr_ptr_sync1  =  gray2bin(wr_gray_sync1)
+#     rd_word[gi]   =  mem_l[rd_ptr_l[gi]]   ;# payload read, pointer-qualified
+# The module's own header states the intent (its line 49): "CDC: wr_ptr crosses
+# to out_clk as GRAY (RX-audit Finding #2 fix, 2026-06-09)".
+#
+# SO TWO DIFFERENT INSTRUMENTS, AND CONFLATING THEM IS THE WHOLE TRAP:
+#
+#   (a) THE DEMET FIRST STAGE gets a false_path. Its D pin is where a
+#       deliberately-unsynchronised value is sampled; the setup/hold check there
+#       is one STA is not entitled to make and hold-fixing it is meaningless
+#       work. ONLY stage 0. wr_gray_sync1's D is fed by wr_gray_sync0's Q in the
+#       SAME domain and IS the metastability settling window -- cutting it would
+#       destroy the protection rather than describe it.
+#
+#   (b) THE PAYLOAD gets a DATAPATH BOUND, never a false path. This is verbatim
+#       the reasoning already in constraints.sdc:522-534 for C2: "The payload
+#       itself ... crosses with NO synchroniser on it at all, and that is
+#       correct by design ... Cutting those paths outright would be wrong;
+#       timing them against an unrelated edge is also wrong."
+#
+# WHAT LEAVING IT ALONE COSTS, so this is not filed as a tidiness fix. All eight
+# word clocks are declared -source TL_CLK_RX -divide_by 16, i.e. IDENTICAL
+# waveforms, so STA sees launch and capture on the same edge: setup gets the
+# full 160 ns and is never the issue, but HOLD gets a ZERO-ns budget against
+# whatever lane-to-lane skew CTS actually built. And CTS built the lanes very
+# differently -- reports/cts_clock_trees.rep:185-192 shows D2D_RX_WORDN_CLK_0
+# with 501 clock gates and lanes 1-7 with 36 each. The hold fixer chases that
+# skew across 4096 FIFO memory flops and a 32:1 read mux, inserting buffers into
+# the receive datapath of the one interface with a known marginal-eye failure
+# mode.
+
+set _dsk "$GPIO/u_deskew"
+
+# The eight word clocks, rebuilt locally: this file is sourced BEFORE
+# constraints.sdc builds $_rx_grp, so that variable does not exist yet.
+set _dsk_wclk {}
+foreach n {0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7} { lappend _dsk_wclk "D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_$n" }
+if {[llength $_dsk_wclk] != 8} {
+    error "tidelink_constraints.sdc: deskew word-clock list built wrong -\
+           [llength $_dsk_wclk], expected 8."
+}
+
+# --- CANDIDATE-LADDER BINDING, AND WHY IT IS NOT OVER-ENGINEERING -----------
+# u_deskew is UNGROUPED during synthesis. In the shipping netlist the flops are
+# flat names inside WavD2DGpio -- `u_deskew_wr_gray_sync0_reg[0][0]`,
+# `u_deskew_g_lane_write[6].mem_l_reg[26][2]` -- while at Genus read time
+# (post-elaborate, pre-map) u_deskew is still a hierarchy level and the
+# separator is `/`. A glob `*` does not cross `/`, so ONE spelling cannot cover
+# both, and this file is read pre-map while the SDC Genus writes is read
+# post-map.
+#
+# DO NOT "SIMPLIFY" THIS TO THE fc_shell IDIOM the block SDC uses:
+#     get_cells -hier -filter {NAME =~ "*gpiorx_*/link_data_pad_clk_reg*"}
+# In Genus, `-filter name` checks the instance's BASE NAME, not its path
+# (Genus 21.1 SDC Command Reference, get_cells: "-filter '{base_name|name}
+# {==|!=|!~} name' -- base_name or name checks the base name of the instance").
+# A pattern containing `/` can never match a base name, so that form returns an
+# EMPTY collection in Genus and the constraint silently does nothing. The
+# hierarchical-path form with a trailing glob is the one this file has already
+# PROVEN binds here (the div_en_r*/Q anchors at line ~145 and the
+# count_reg[3]/Q anchors at line ~320, both measured 8/8 at read time).
+#
+# ERROR ON ZERO, WARN ON COUNT. A zero bind is fatal: it is the failure this
+# whole file exists to prevent -- an exception that reads as handled and
+# constrains nothing. A count that differs from the shipping build's is loud but
+# not fatal, because Genus may legitimately merge or prune flops.
+
+# group name / mandatory? / measured count in build/full-20260814 / candidates
+set _dsk_demet [list \
+  [list "wr_gray_sync0 (FIFO write pointer, gray)"  1 48 [list \
+     "$_dsk/wr_gray_sync0_reg*/D"   "$_dsk/wr_gray_sync0*/D" \
+     "${_dsk}_wr_gray_sync0_reg*/D"]] \
+  [list "sync_idx_sync0 (SYNC re-anchor index)"     0 48 [list \
+     "$_dsk/g_sync_sync.sync_idx_sync0_reg*/D"   "$_dsk/g_sync_sync/sync_idx_sync0_reg*/D" \
+     "$_dsk/sync_idx_sync0_reg*/D"               "${_dsk}_g_sync_sync.sync_idx_sync0_reg*/D"]] \
+  [list "sync_seen_sync0 (SYNC re-anchor valid)"    0  8 [list \
+     "$_dsk/g_sync_sync.sync_seen_sync0_reg*/D"  "$_dsk/g_sync_sync/sync_seen_sync0_reg*/D" \
+     "$_dsk/sync_seen_sync0_reg*/D"              "${_dsk}_g_sync_sync.sync_seen_sync0_reg*/D"]] \
+  [list "sync_dist_sync0 (SYNC Hamming obs)"        0 40 [list \
+     "$_dsk/g_sync_dist_sync.sync_dist_sync0_reg*/D"  "$_dsk/g_sync_dist_sync/sync_dist_sync0_reg*/D" \
+     "$_dsk/sync_dist_sync0_reg*/D"                   "${_dsk}_g_sync_dist_sync.sync_dist_sync0_reg*/D"]] \
+]
+
+set _dsk_cut 0
+foreach _e $_dsk_demet {
+    foreach {_nm _must _exp _cands} $_e { break }
+    set _p {}
+    foreach _c $_cands {
+        set _p [get_pins -quiet $_c]
+        if {[sizeof_collection $_p] > 0} { break }
+    }
+    if {[sizeof_collection $_p] == 0} {
+        if {$_must} {
+            error "tidelink_constraints.sdc: deskew demet anchor '$_nm' matched\
+ NOTHING under any candidate spelling ([join $_cands {, }]). The deskew FIFO's\
+ pointer CDC would be timed as a synchronous check and hold-fixed across the D2D\
+ receive datapath, while this block reads as though it were handled. Do NOT\
+ waive this by deleting the constraint - find the spelling. See the RX\
+ word-clock anchors above and why 16,653 flops went untimed."
+        } else {
+            puts "TIDELINK-SDC: NOTE deskew demet '$_nm' absent - skipped."
+            puts "TIDELINK-SDC:      Legitimate ONLY if SYNC_REANCHOR_EN=0 in this"
+            puts "TIDELINK-SDC:      build (the whole g_sync_capture/g_sync_sync tree"
+            puts "TIDELINK-SDC:      is generate-pruned there). If SYNC_REANCHOR IS on,"
+            puts "TIDELINK-SDC:      this is a REAL GAP - the hierarchy moved."
+            continue
+        }
+    }
+    if {[sizeof_collection $_p] != $_exp} {
+        puts "**WARN: tidelink_constraints.sdc: deskew demet '$_nm' bound\
+ [sizeof_collection $_p] pins, expected $_exp (measured in build/full-20260814).\
+ Not fatal - Genus may merge or prune - but check the hierarchy did not move."
+    }
+    # -from the word clocks, -to NAMED PINS. This is a clock-to-PIN exception,
+    # the same instrument as constraints.sdc:517-518, NOT a clock-to-clock cut:
+    # the C5 doctrine at the top of constraints.sdc is honoured.
+    #
+    # LANE 0 IS DEGENERATE AND THAT IS ACCEPTED. out_clk IS D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_0,
+    # so lane 0's pointer "crossing" is same-clock and this also cuts a path
+    # that would always have passed. Cutting it costs no coverage - the same
+    # logic is replicated per lane and lanes 1-7 are cut regardless - and
+    # excluding lane 0 would need a lane-discriminating pattern, which is
+    # exactly the fragile spelling this ladder exists to avoid.
+    set_false_path -from [get_clocks $_dsk_wclk] -to $_p
+    incr _dsk_cut
+    puts "TIDELINK-SDC: deskew demet cut '$_nm' - [sizeof_collection $_p] pins"
+}
+
+# --- THE REVERSE CROSSING, which is easy to miss entirely -------------------
+# sync_obs_clr_i is generated in out_clk and lands on a 3-flop demet inside EACH
+# lane's OWN write clock (tidelink_lane_deskew_v2.sv:573-582, clr_meta_l ->
+# clr_sync_l -> clr_d_l). Same instrument, opposite direction: cut stage 0 only.
+set _dsk_clr {}
+foreach _c [list "$_dsk/g_lane_write*.g_sync_capture.clr_meta_l_reg*/D" \
+                 "$_dsk/g_lane_write*/g_sync_capture/clr_meta_l_reg*/D" \
+                 "${_dsk}_g_lane_write*.g_sync_capture.clr_meta_l_reg*/D"] {
+    set _dsk_clr [get_pins -quiet $_c]
+    if {[sizeof_collection $_dsk_clr] > 0} { break }
+}
+if {[sizeof_collection $_dsk_clr] == 0} {
+    puts "TIDELINK-SDC: NOTE deskew clr_meta_l demet absent - skipped\
+ (expected only when SYNC_REANCHOR_EN=0)."
+} else {
+    if {[sizeof_collection $_dsk_clr] != 8} {
+        puts "**WARN: tidelink_constraints.sdc: deskew clr_meta_l bound\
+ [sizeof_collection $_dsk_clr] pins, expected 8."
+    }
+    set_false_path -from [get_clocks D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_0] -to $_dsk_clr
+    puts "TIDELINK-SDC: deskew clr_meta_l demet cut -\
+ [sizeof_collection $_dsk_clr] pins"
+}
+
+# --- THE PAYLOAD: A DATAPATH BOUND, NOT A FALSE PATH ------------------------
+# mem_l is 8 lanes x 32 entries x 16 bits = 4096 flops, written in lane_clk[gi]
+# and read combinationally in out_clk through a 32:1 mux
+# (tidelink_lane_deskew_v2.sv:542/549). It has no synchroniser by design and
+# must not get one: the gray pointer's value is what guarantees the entry is
+# stable before the read side addresses it.
+#
+# THE BUDGET IS ONE UI, $D2D_LINK_PERIOD = 10.0 ns, AND IT IS CHOSEN TO
+# DISCRIMINATE. The destination cycle is 160 ns; a bound at one destination
+# cycle -- the number the C2 block uses for its own payload -- would be a
+# ceiling nothing could ever touch, i.e. a check that measures nothing. The
+# protocol floor is looser still (the 2-flop pointer sync means the read side
+# never addresses an entry written less than 2 x 160 ns ago). A 65nm 32:1 mux
+# plus routing is order 1-2 ns, so 10 ns leaves 5-10x headroom and will not
+# force optimisation effort, while still catching a pathological read path or a
+# hold-buffer chain that a mis-timed hold fix threaded into the FIFO output.
+#
+# PLAIN set_max_delay, NOT -datapath_only, AND NOT -ignore_clock_latency.
+#   * -datapath_only DOES NOT EXIST IN EITHER TOOL HERE. Verified against the
+#     shipping references, not assumed: Genus 21.1 SDC Command Reference lists
+#     set_max_delay's options as [-rise] [-fall] [-ignore_clock_latency]
+#     [-exception_name] [-comment] [-combinational_from_to] [-reset_path] and
+#     the string "datapath_only" appears ZERO times in the whole document;
+#     Innovus 21.11 Text Command Reference gives
+#     `set_max_delay value [-combinational_from_to | -ignore_clock_latency]`.
+#     -datapath_only is PrimeTime-only. (This is also why the C2 block's
+#     catch-wrapped -datapath_only at constraints.sdc:568-570 ALWAYS takes its
+#     fallback leg in this flow. That is safe -- the fallback is stricter -- but
+#     it means the C2 payload bound is not the datapath-only bound its comment
+#     describes. Flagged, deliberately not changed here.)
+#   * -ignore_clock_latency IS supported by both, but it is not needed and it
+#     drags in two Innovus globals whose defaults are `false`
+#     (timing_constraint_path_delay_exclude_{check,io}_delay_from_ignore_clock_latency),
+#     i.e. check-arc and I/O delays stay INSIDE the slack computation. Charging
+#     clock latency instead is STRICTER, never looser, and 10 ns has the room.
+#
+# AND AN EXPLICIT set_min_delay 0, WHICH IS THE HALF THAT ACTUALLY MATTERS.
+# set_max_delay alone bounds setup; whether it also displaces the clock-derived
+# HOLD check on the same paths is not stated in either tool's reference, and the
+# hold check is the one doing the damage here. Declaring the min requirement
+# explicitly as 0 says what is true of a pointer-protected payload -- there is
+# no hold relationship to meet -- in a form neither tool can interpret two ways.
+# Genus records that it does not time set_min_delay itself but "will be written
+# out using write_sdc", so Innovus is where it takes effect. That is correct:
+# Innovus is where hold fixing happens.
+set _dsk_mem {}
+foreach _c [list "$_dsk/g_lane_write*mem_l_reg*" "$_dsk/g_lane_write*/mem_l_reg*" \
+                 "${_dsk}_g_lane_write*mem_l_reg*" "$_dsk/mem_l_reg*"] {
+    set _dsk_mem [get_cells -quiet $_c]
+    if {[sizeof_collection $_dsk_mem] > 0} { break }
+}
+if {[sizeof_collection $_dsk_mem] == 0} {
+    error "tidelink_constraints.sdc: deskew payload anchor mem_l matched NOTHING.\
+ The 4096 FIFO memory flops would be timed as a synchronous word-to-word\
+ crossing and hold-fixed across the D2D receive datapath. Refusing to continue."
+}
+if {[sizeof_collection $_dsk_mem] != 4096} {
+    puts "**WARN: tidelink_constraints.sdc: deskew mem_l bound\
+ [sizeof_collection $_dsk_mem] cells, expected 4096 (8 lanes x 32 entries x 16\
+ bits, measured in build/full-20260814). Check DEPTH_LOG has not moved."
+}
+set_max_delay $D2D_LINK_PERIOD -from $_dsk_mem -to [get_clocks D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_0]
+set_min_delay 0                -from $_dsk_mem -to [get_clocks D2D_RX_WORD_CLK_0]
+puts "TIDELINK-SDC: deskew payload bounded -\
+ [sizeof_collection $_dsk_mem] mem_l cells, max $D2D_LINK_PERIOD ns / min 0"
+
+if {$_dsk_cut < 1} {
+    error "tidelink_constraints.sdc: deskew block cut $_dsk_cut demet groups.\
+ At least the mandatory wr_gray_sync0 group must have bound."
